{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-45164-r4514948","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Chicken Riggies","sourcePageId":45164,"sourceRevision":"4514948","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T02:54:11Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Chicken%20Riggies&oldid=4514948","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:22.708Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using chicken breast","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using cream","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using olive","Category:Recipes using parmesan","Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:United States recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d54d66a59675b3c3f8fc601677f2fbbb91117ef384b5594fbd41b33192b12a84","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chicken recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|Cuisine of the United States]]\n\n'''Chicken Riggies''' (recipe by P.A. Johnson) is a Utica, NY classic. It is well known throughout the greater Mohawk Valley and once a year there is a festival in honor of this dish called Riggiefest, held to benefit the YWCA of the Mohawk Valley. Here is a recipe based from a Mohawk Valley native:  http://miocibo.com/2008/12/21/chicken-riggies/.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 stick [[cookbook:margarine|margarine]] (not butter), melted\n* 1 [[cookbook:onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 2–5 cloves [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]], minced\n* 1 jar (20 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]) sweet peppers, sliced and seeded\n* 3 sliced hot cherry peppers (jarred ones with oil)\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] grated [[Cookbook:Parmesan Cheese|Parmesan cheese]] \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] boneless [[cookbook:chicken|chicken]] breast, [[Cookbook:Cube|cubed]]\n* 1 can [[cookbook:Chicken Broth|chicken broth]]\n* 1 can (15 oz) [[Cookbook:Tomato Sauce|tomato sauce]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Pint|pint]] [[cookbook:cream|cream]]\n* 1 small can sliced black [[Cookbook:Olive|olives]]\n* 1–1½ lb rigatoni [[cookbook:pasta|pasta]], cooked\n\n==Procedure==\n# [[cookbook:Sauté|Sauté]] onion, peppers, and garlic in the margarine slowly over low/medium heat until the onions are clear.\n# Add the Parmesan, chicken breast, chicken stock, tomato sauce, cream, and olives. [[Cookbook:Simmer|Simmer]] for about an hour.\n# Serve over the cooked pasta.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* It is important to use jarred peppers—the flavor of fresh peppers completely changes the recipe.\n\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken breast]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parmesan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using olive]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chicken Riggies","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 stick margarine (not butter), melted","sourceText":"1 stick margarine (not butter), melted","amountText":"1 stick margarine (not butter), melted","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 onion, minced","sourceText":"1 onion, minced","amountText":"1 onion, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2–5 cloves garlic, minced","sourceText":"2–5 cloves garlic, minced","amountText":"2–5 cloves garlic, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 jar (20 oz) sweet peppers, sliced and seeded","sourceText":"1 jar (20 oz) sweet peppers, sliced and seeded","amountText":"1 jar (20 oz) sweet peppers, sliced and seeded","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"3 sliced hot cherry peppers (jarred ones with oil)","sourceText":"3 sliced hot cherry peppers (jarred ones with oil)","amountText":"3 sliced hot cherry peppers (jarred ones with oil)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 cup grated Parmesan cheese","sourceText":"1 cup grated Parmesan cheese","amountText":"1 cup grated Parmesan cheese","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 lb boneless chicken breast, cubed","sourceText":"2 lb boneless chicken breast, cubed","amountText":"2 lb boneless chicken breast, cubed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 can chicken broth","sourceText":"1 can chicken broth","amountText":"1 can chicken broth","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 can (15 oz) tomato sauce","sourceText":"1 can (15 oz) tomato sauce","amountText":"1 can (15 oz) tomato sauce","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"½ pint cream","sourceText":"½ pint cream","amountText":"½ pint cream","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"so